WEBVTT FILE

1
00:00.179 --> 00:03.472
This is the American Forces Network in Paris.

2
00:03.497 --> 00:07.279
A pall of black destruction and chaos still hangs over Hiroshima.

3
00:07.304 --> 00:09.325
Events are now moving swiftly.

4
00:09.350 --> 00:12.324
The President... - Hey, Maurice! Leave it on!

5
00:12.349 --> 00:13.518
Did you hear the news?

6
00:13.543 --> 00:15.191
First things first.

7
00:15.216 --> 00:17.383
It'll take more one bomb to end this caper.

8
00:17.408 --> 00:21.086
One will get you twenty, it's over in a week.  Will you cover $60 bucks worth?  You got it.

9
00:21.087 --> 00:22.769
Don't do it.

10
00:22.794 --> 00:24.946
Barney just came from the office.

11
00:24.971 --> 00:29.286
Japan offered to surrender if...  - What! Where!  - if we let the Emperor stay in his throne.

12
00:29.311 --> 00:30.013
When are we going home?

13
00:30.038 --> 00:32.446
Charlie, what's the dope on discharges?

14
00:32.471 --> 00:37.046
Well, if you start right now you're already behind 10,000 other guys.

15
00:41.868 --> 00:45.249
I'll have to get right back to the office. Why?

16
00:45.274 --> 00:47.886
I tried to phone you.

17
00:47.911 --> 00:51.061
Don't ever phone me if you can possibly come yourself.

18
00:51.086 --> 00:54.553
And don't ever leave if you can stay.

19
00:56.911 --> 01:00.268
Maybe we can meet for late supper or something.

20
01:00.293 --> 01:01.284
We'll see.

21
01:04.748 --> 01:07.768
Is it really over? The war?

22
01:07.793 --> 01:15.168
Because I want to buy you silk shirts and silk socks and silk shorts.

23
01:15.193 --> 01:19.651
Oh, darling!

24
01:28.286 --> 01:30.804
Taxi!

25
01:32.971 --> 01:35.566
What did you do with my umbrella?

26
01:35.591 --> 01:39.698
I had it when I started over here and stopped a second. Must have lost it.

27
01:39.699 --> 01:41.879
We've got a Special Edition coming out.

28
01:41.904 --> 01:43.187
You had better hurry.

29
01:43.212 --> 01:45.327
I'll get you a taxi first. Taxi!

30
01:45.352 --> 01:48.509
Now you stop fussing about me.

31
01:48.510 --> 01:50.862
Will you will you wait for me?

32
01:50.863 --> 01:53.793
I think I'll go home early and give Daddy a shock.

33
01:53.818 --> 01:54.926
But in this rain?

34
01:54.927 --> 02:00.293
I may not be able to cook and to sew, but I really can find myself a taxi.

35
02:00.294 --> 02:02.936
It's the first thing I learned at finishing school.

36
02:02.937 --> 02:03.993
Now you go on ahead.

37
02:04.018 --> 02:06.109
You're a girl after my own heart.

38
02:06.110 --> 02:10.271
Make no mistake about it. I'm after it, all right.

39
02:26.124 --> 02:30.130
Taxi!

40
02:39.369 --> 02:43.636
Violets.

41
02:44.749 --> 02:47.662
Merci!

42
02:52.395 --> 02:54.505
Marion!

43
02:54.837 --> 02:58.327
I phoned, and they said it was all right for visitors.

44
02:58.352 --> 03:00.419
Did she get my flowers?

45
03:00.444 --> 03:02.407
Every day.

46
03:02.432 --> 03:04.321
All my messages?

47
03:04.346 --> 03:06.871
Every one.

48
03:06.872 --> 03:09.108
Can I go in now?

49
03:10.168 --> 03:13.714
Charles! - What?

50
03:24.835 --> 03:27.315
Hi!

51
03:27.316 --> 03:29.417
How do feel?

52
03:29.442 --> 03:32.060
The nurse answers all the stark questions.

53
03:32.061 --> 03:37.027
The patient improves, but it is required not to really hurt.

54
03:37.052 --> 03:41.839
I was going to ask you to dance, but I guess that's out, huh?

55
03:42.977 --> 03:46.250
I was expecting a younger, more attractive nurse.

56
03:46.275 --> 03:48.765
She's the fourth in two weeks.

57
03:48.790 --> 03:51.144
Daddy's a pincher.

58
04:02.225 --> 04:06.758
For heaven sakes, get that guilty look off your face.

59
04:06.783 --> 04:09.193
I lost your umbrella.

60
04:09.217 --> 04:11.196
I gave you the flu.

61
04:11.197 --> 04:12.744
Don't be silly.

62
04:12.769 --> 04:16.072
It was raining, I got wet, so I got the flu.

63
04:16.073 --> 04:18.484
And it's not your fault.

64
04:20.266 --> 04:23.840
I was wondering how you would look out of uniform.

65
04:23.865 --> 04:27.415
Even better.

66
04:27.416 --> 04:29.148
It's my fault.

67
04:29.173 --> 04:31.006
I would have caught this, anyway.

68
04:31.031 --> 04:33.919
I catch cold even from weather forecasts.

69
04:33.944 --> 04:37.559
Thank you for the lovely flowers. - Oh!

70
04:39.605 --> 04:41.862
What's the matter?

71
04:41.863 --> 04:43.599
I don't know.

72
04:43.624 --> 04:48.512
You look so pale and sweet and priceless.

73
04:48.550 --> 04:51.826
Remember, the nurse is right outside the door.

74
04:51.850 --> 04:54.690
Not that I'll call her.

75
04:59.617 --> 05:05.551
One thing I learned these last weeks, I love you.

76
05:05.576 --> 05:08.472
You loved me the first day.

77
05:08.497 --> 05:10.405
I did?

78
05:10.406 --> 05:12.059
You sure did.

79
05:12.084 --> 05:14.425
We should have told each other then.

80
05:14.450 --> 05:18.545
Look at all headway we could have made.

81
05:19.538 --> 05:24.592
For the first time in my life, I wish I had lots of money.

82
05:24.617 --> 05:27.558
Oh, money!

83
05:27.583 --> 05:31.691
Daddy says it isn't what you have, it's what you owe.

84
05:31.716 --> 05:34.224
I don't even owe enough.

85
05:34.249 --> 05:37.484
And what are your prospects young man?

86
05:37.509 --> 05:39.419
Prospects?

87
05:39.420 --> 05:42.184
My old job on the news at 65 a week.

88
05:42.209 --> 05:43.331
Please!

89
05:43.362 --> 05:46.977
I'm only suppose to think beautiful thoughts.

90
05:48.265 --> 05:53.552
Doesn't DuPont or General Motors need a president or something?

91
05:53.577 --> 05:59.580
Well, the Paris office of the Europa News Service needs a reporter.

92
05:59.605 --> 06:02.013
Paris!

93
06:02.038 --> 06:04.348
It doesn't pay as much as the New York job.

94
06:04.349 --> 06:08.493
But you don't need money to have fun in Paris.

95
06:08.494 --> 06:13.386
Yeah, yeah.

96
06:13.411 --> 06:16.061
Well, I've been working on a book.

97
06:16.086 --> 06:18.439
I should get back to the States. Why can't you write your book here?

98
06:18.464 --> 06:24.322
Oh, Charlie, darling, please marry me and let's stay here. Please?

99
06:24.347 --> 06:28.160
Oh, it sounds so wonderful.

100
06:28.204 --> 06:32.853
But isn't it a little crazy?

101
06:35.275 --> 06:38.982
Yes, it is crazy.

102
06:39.007 --> 06:45.775
If you had any sense, you would walk right out that door and never see me or call me again.

103
06:45.915 --> 06:51.834
Maybe send back my umbrella and call it quits.

104
06:51.835 --> 06:58.306
But I haven't any sense. No sense at all.

105
07:06.243 --> 07:08.891
You have no sense.

106
07:08.922 --> 07:12.177
I have a one degree temperature.

107
07:12.202 --> 07:17.502
If I were 98.6, this would never happen.

108
07:29.325 --> 07:34.344
Forgive me, but, uh, I'm rather enjoying playing the anxious father.

109
07:34.345 --> 07:36.463
After all, it's Helen's first marriage, you know.

110
07:36.488 --> 07:38.349
Only marriage, sir. Tut, tut!

111
07:38.374 --> 07:39.616
No arrogance, please.

112
07:39.641 --> 07:43.024
Helen tells me that you are a very seriousminded person.

113
07:43.025 --> 07:46.048
You know, both feet on the ground, hard working, industrious.

114
07:46.049 --> 07:47.579
Well, I try to be, sir.

115
07:47.580 --> 07:51.935
I tell you, frankly, these are not the qualities I'd hope for in a son-in-law.

116
07:51.960 --> 07:54.798
I'll uh, go even further.

117
07:54.799 --> 07:57.711
They're, uh, not the qualities to make Helen happy.

118
07:57.712 --> 08:01.436
Oh, well, sir, I uh I'm going to work on a Paris news agency.

119
08:01.437 --> 08:04.229
I'll be surrounded by carefree, irresponsible characters.

120
08:04.230 --> 08:06.653
Some of it is bound to rub off on me.

121
08:06.654 --> 08:08.205
Well, let us hope so.

122
08:08.230 --> 08:12.711
Tell me, do I... do I strike you as being an unusual father?

123
08:12.736 --> 08:14.721
You certainly do.

124
08:14.722 --> 08:17.311
That's a very straightforward answer.

125
08:17.336 --> 08:19.339
I'm trying to overcome this tendency.

126
08:19.364 --> 08:22.470
You understand, of course, that I can't afford to give you a large wedding.

127
08:22.471 --> 08:24.341
I don't care for one, thanks.

128
08:24.366 --> 08:25.497
Care for a drink?

129
08:25.521 --> 08:27.997
Oh, yes. I'd love one, thank you.

130
08:27.998 --> 08:31.891
Oh, that's too bad. You know, I'm getting a little low on this stuff and I was... - Oh, that's all right, I'll...

131
08:31.892 --> 08:32.763
Here you are.

132
08:32.764 --> 08:33.799
Oh, thank you.

133
08:33.824 --> 08:36.092
Do you know what you're getting for a wedding present?

134
08:36.117 --> 08:38.596
Well, Helen told me what not to expect.

135
08:38.621 --> 08:42.390
My dear, sir, you are getting the old family joke.

136
08:42.415 --> 08:45.943
4,000 acres of invaluable oil land.

137
08:45.968 --> 08:47.310
Thank you, very much, sir.

138
08:47.311 --> 08:48.663
Not at all.

139
08:48.694 --> 08:54.249
You know, after all it's not bad being an oil baron, even if there's no oil, uh?

140
09:00.636 --> 09:04.379
Well, did you give Helen your permission?

141
09:04.380 --> 09:06.582
I had to give her my permission. - Huh?

142
09:06.607 --> 09:09.415
Claude has asked me do be the mother of his children.

143
09:09.440 --> 09:12.428
Really? That... that that seems a bit irregular, doesn't it?

144
09:12.453 --> 09:15.734
Dad, Claude has asked her to marry him.

145
09:15.759 --> 09:18.127
Oh!

146
09:18.152 --> 09:25.920
Well, then I suppose I must kiss you.

147
09:26.920 --> 09:32.700
Do you, uh, say best wishes to the bride? Or congratulations to the groom? Or which way is it? I've forgotten.

148
09:32.731 --> 09:35.713
You just go ahead and kiss each other.

149
09:49.511 --> 09:54.151
What did you put into that kiss?

150
09:54.176 --> 09:58.418
Well, why don't you come here and find out.

151
10:01.931 --> 10:07.373
Helen, getting married, Marion getting married.

152
10:07.374 --> 10:11.949
A father abandoned in middle age.

153
10:11.974 --> 10:15.946
What man could ask for more.